### Impact of higher interest rates {#sec-plustaux}

The variant presented in this section is based on higher interest rates from 2028, namely the rate observed in September 2026 (4.5%). In this case, the long-term interest–growth differential is 1.7 percentage points.

The impact is substantial: the cumulative effort is 4.2% of GDP, i.e. an additional €24 billion at 2026 GDP relative to the reference scenario (@tbl-optimal1), in which debt stands at 115.6% in 2025. The average output loss is 0.2 point higher than the reference scenario.

Between this scenario (high rates) and the previous one (lower rates), the difference in cumulative adjustment is of the order of €33 billion (at 2026 GDP) and 0.3 point of average output loss.


